      <ul>
      <li>In {"{"}{"{"} olmv0 {"}"}{"}"}, the successor closest to the channel head is chosen.</li>
      <li>In {"{"}{"{"} olmv1 {"}"}{"}"}, the successor with the highest semantic version (semver) is chosen.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
      Consider the following set of file-based catalog (FBC) channel entries:
      <CodeBlock code={"# ...\n- name: example.v3.0.0\n  skips: [\"example.v2.0.0\"]\n- name: example.v2.0.0\n  skipRange: >=1.0.0 <2.0.0"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>If <code>1.0.0</code> is installed, {"{"}{"{"} olmv1 {"}"}{"}"} behavior differs in the following ways:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>{"{"}{"{"} olmv0_caps {"}"}{"}"} will not detect an update path to <code>v2.0.0</code> because <code>v2.0.0</code> is skipped and not on the <code>replaces</code> chain.</li>
      <li>{"{"}{"{"} olmv1 {"}"}{"}"} will detect the update path because {"{"}{"{"} olmv1 {"}"}{"}"} does not have a concept of a <code>replaces</code> chain. {"{"}{"{"} olmv1 {"}"}{"}"} finds all entries that have a <code>replace</code>, <code>skip</code>, or <code>skipRange</code> value that covers the currently installed version.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
